  "body": "**Description:**\r\n\r\n<!-- Describe here the feature you are requesting. -->\r\nWhile room administrators can specify the privilege level of other participants (admin/moderator/etc), they have no control over invitation of new members (other than the ability to remove them after they join). There should be options to restrict this, especially in private encrypted rooms. There may be usage cases where it is desirable for historical chat data to be available to trusted new participants, but not to participants invited by an ignorant existing member. In such cases a malicious source could socially engineer a room member into sending them an invite and grab the whole chat before the admin deletes them.\r\n\r\nRequested options:\r\n\r\nRestrict inviting capability to room owner only\r\nRestrict inviting capability to users with given access level [drop-down list: admin/moderator/etc]\r\nRequire invites to be approved unanimously by all members\r\nRequire session verification to be unanimous\r\n\r\nThis options should be available for private rooms, possibly also for public encrypted rooms (topic for discussion)",
